const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"论文考察过去一段时间表现较好的股票与表现较差的股票，之后是否仍出现系统性的相对收益差。 阅读时先把它理解为一个被界定的问题，而不是可以脱离样本、时间和制度环境的结论。",en:"“Returns to Buying Winners and Selling Losers: Implications for Stock Market Efficiency” frames a bounded research question. Read the stated question together with the named sample, dates, and institutional setting rather than treating it as a conclusion that automatically travels to another market or period."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1540-6261.1993.tb04702.x",label:{zh:"The Journal of Finance (1993) · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Finance (1993) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"公开说明以形成期与持有期组合为核心，比较赢家与输家组合在不同时间跨度内的后续收益。 这说明比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系是研究合同的一部分；改变其中任何一项，都可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"For “Returns to Buying Winners and Selling Losers: Implications for Stock Market Efficiency”, the source describes a deliberate comparison, observation window, and control relation. Those choices are part of its research contract: changing one can change the proposition being tested, even when the method label remains the same."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1540-6261.1993.tb04702.x",label:{zh:"The Journal of Finance (1993) · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Finance (1993) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"关键对象是复权收益、形成与持有窗口、证券样本和组合构造日期，而不是一句“动量”标签。 数据字段、可得时点和样本筛选需要与原始研究分开记录，不能仅凭同名变量或最终修订数据就视为可比。",en:"For “Returns to Buying Winners and Selling Losers: Implications for Stock Market Efficiency”, keep the fields, their availability timing, and the sample filters separate from the original study. A same-named variable, later-revised database, or matching end-of-period date is not automatically a comparable input."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1540-6261.1993.tb04702.x",label:{zh:"The Journal of Finance (1993) · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Finance (1993) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"来源描述的是对市场效率含义的经验检验，重点在相对组合回报与其随持有期变化的表现。 它支持的是该来源所描述的经验或理论关系；它本身不把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"For “Returns to Buying Winners and Selling Losers: Implications for Stock Market Efficiency”, the source supports only the empirical or theoretical relation it describes. It does not turn association, model fit, or historical performance into causality, a directly executable procedure, or a guarantee about subsequent outcomes."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1540-6261.1993.tb04702.x",label:{zh:"The Journal of Finance (1993) · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Finance (1993) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"明确收益是否包含退市、如何处理重叠持有期、何时形成组合，以及是否使用当时可得的证券范围。 在做后续分析前，应把这些选择写入版本化的研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"Before extending “Returns to Buying Winners and Selling Losers: Implications for Stock Market Efficiency”, record its sample, timing, construction choices, and source edition in a versioned note. Keep the primary-source link and access date so a later reader can distinguish a changed definition from a changed result."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1540-6261.1993.tb04702.x",label:{zh:"The Journal of Finance (1993) · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Finance (1993) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 The Journal of Finance (1993)。历史组合差异不能替代交易成本、可借券性、容量或另一个市场的可实现收益评估。 若需要量化结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites The Journal of Finance (1993) for “Returns to Buying Winners and Selling Losers: Implications for Stock Market Efficiency”. Its public description defines the boundary. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1540-6261.1993.tb04702.x",label:{zh:"The Journal of Finance (1993) · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Finance (1993) · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“Returns to Buying Winners and Selling Losers: Implications for Stock Market Efficiency”所公开说明的研究问题与设计边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。历史组合差异不能替代交易成本、可借券性、容量或另一个市场的可实现收益评估。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “Returns to Buying Winners and Selling Losers: Implications for Stock Market Efficiency”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
